|lore=“What was that?” The Jedi power known as ‘affect mind’ is often used to create minor distractions, allowing Jedi to elude enemies rather than engage them in battle.
|game_text=Plays on table. Bad Feeling Have I is canceled. Unless Inner Strength on table, opponent may use only one combat card per turn. Let Them Make The First Move may target only Undercover spies and R2-D2.
|errata_history=This is the original printing: the earliest PC card image of this card (8 July 2018). It is not the last version; the last version before the card was cut is [[Affect Mind (V) (Virtual Set D) (Errata)]] (PC-E1). The image is the PC card image of this version.
* '''Original''' (this page): PC card image of 8 July 2018<ref name="ht-L_affectmind-0">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/022435b/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Light/large/affectmind.gif affectmind.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/022435b 022435b] (8 July 2018, “Set 9 load”).</ref>, no errata mark; lower-left name “•Affect Mind”. The PC first released this shield with [[Virtual Set 0]] / [[Virtual Set D]] on 24 September 2014. The PC's Holotable image set starts on 8 July 2018, so this is the earliest surviving PC card image; whether the 2014 release slip had the same words is not shown by it. Text: “Plays on table. Bad Feeling Have I is canceled. Unless Inner Strength on table, opponent may use only one combat card per turn. Let Them Make The First Move may target only Undercover spies and R2-D2.”
* '''PC-E1''' ([[Affect Mind (V) (Virtual Set D) (Errata)]]): PC card image of 31 July 2022<ref name="ht-L_affectmind-1">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/ab74419/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Light/large/affectmind.gif affectmind.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/ab74419 ab74419] (31 July 2022, “updated hires gifs”); high-resolution image <code>ResetDS-Light/hires/affectmind.png</code>, commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/594c3a0 594c3a0] (31 July 2022, “Set 0 Hi Res”).</ref>, no errata mark; lower-left name “Affect Mind”. What changed from the previous version: re-rendered by the PC in its high-resolution card style (new frame, colours and typesetting); same words. The bullet is dropped from the lower-left name (“Affect Mind”). No errata mark. The printed errata mark (none) does not match this version's place in the release order (change 1 of this card): recorded as a [[Players Committee transcription errors#Errata marks that do not match the version (Virtual Modern)|PC transcription error]]. Text: “Plays on table. Bad Feeling Have I is canceled. Unless Inner Strength on table, opponent may use only one combat card per turn. Let Them Make The First Move may target only Undercover spies and R2-D2.”
Versions follow Bill's rulings of 12 November 2026: every visible change on a PC card image is a version, numbered in release order; a printed errata mark that does not match that order is recorded as a PC transcription error.
|notes='''Blanked:''' The Players Committee cut this shield from Virtual Set D with [[Virtual Set 23]] on 22 July 2024: the July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit lists “•Affect Mind (V)” under “Light Side – Cut”<ref name="dskit2024">Players Committee, [https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/DShieldUpdateKit_2024_July.pdf July 2024 Defensive Shield Update Kit] (PDF, 3 pages, “SWCCG Players Committee, July 2024”; file built 2 August 2024), released with [[Virtual Set 23]] (22 July 2024).</ref>. The PC card data says its functions moved to other Defensive Shield cards. A blanked card is treated as if it did not exist from that date (in effect a ban); it is not a new version. It stays in its set and is legal in period formats that end before the blanking.
